{
  "version": "v1",
  "description": "Confirmed delivery of consent events (outbox). The per-tool audit log <XDG_STATE_HOME>/<tool>/consent/audit.jsonl is the durable source of truth: every record carries `log` (an id minted when the file is created) and `seq` (1, 2, 3, ... per log). A relay publishes records after the ack cursor <XDG_STATE_HOME>/<tool>/consent/audit.cursor ({\"log\", \"seq\"}, written atomically, 0600) in seq order, as bus events with topic kit.core.consent.<event>, source core.consent, id `<log>:<seq>` (the idempotency key) and the record as payload. A record is delivered when Publish returns nil, i.e. every sync subscriber on the local bus returned nil; the cursor then moves past it. A failure stops the flush at that record. At-least-once: a record published but not yet acked (crash, cursor write failure, subscriber error) is published again with the same key; acked records are never resent. A cursor naming another log is ignored; a corrupt cursor fails the flush.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "each record gets the next sequence number and is delivered once acked",
      "now": "2026-03-01T00:00:00Z",
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "record",
          "record": {
            "event": "granted",
            "capability": "io.screen.capture",
            "subject": "app:dek",
            "decision": "allow",
            "duration": "always",
            "decision_source": "prompt",
            "prompt_version": 1
          },
          "expect": {
            "seq": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "record",
          "record": {
            "event": "used",
            "capability": "io.screen.capture",
            "subject": "app:dek",
            "decision": "allow",
            "duration": "always",
            "decision_source": "prompt",
            "prompt_version": 1
          },
          "expect": {
            "seq": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "flush",
          "expect": {
            "delivered": [
              1,
              2
            ],
            "cursor": 2,
            "pending": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "op": "flush",
          "expect": {
            "delivered": [],
            "cursor": 2,
            "pending": 0
          }
        }
      ],
      "published": [
        {
          "seq": 1,
          "topic": "kit.core.consent.granted"
        },
        {
          "seq": 2,
          "topic": "kit.core.consent.used"
        }
      ],
      "cursor_file": {
        "seq": 2
      }
    },
